# Relief Network (v2) — environment

# --- Data ingestion (npm run ingest) ---------------------------------------
# Default source is the bundled snapshot data/backup-lbresponse-db.json.
# To mirror the LIVE Firebase Realtime Database instead, run:
#   npm run ingest -- --source=firebase
# and provide the credentials below (authorized live source: collreliefnetwork).
FIREBASE_DB_URL=https://collreliefnetwork-default-rtdb.europe-west1.firebasedatabase.app
# Path to the Firebase service-account JSON (kept OUT of git). Defaults to the
# old backend's copy if unset: ../lbresponse-api/service-account.json
# FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT=/absolute/path/to/service-account.json

# --- Database (Prisma) ------------------------------------------------------
# SQLite. Relative file: paths are resolved against the schema dir (prisma/),
# so `file:./dev.db` is prisma/dev.db. The Docker images override this to an
# absolute path on the mounted volume: DATABASE_URL=file:/data/relief.db
DATABASE_URL=file:./dev.db

# --- Runtime ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Port the production server listens on (pm2 / next start).
PORT=3000
# Bind address; 0.0.0.0 exposes the app on the server's public IP.
HOSTNAME=0.0.0.0

# --- Analytics (Umami, optional) -------------------------------------------
# Self-hosted, cookieless product analytics. BOTH must be set for the tracker
# to load; leaving them unset (the default) means no tracking — which is why
# local dev never reports. Infra provides these once Umami is live; the
# website-id differs per environment (prod vs testing). Honors Do-Not-Track.
# See docs/ANALYTICS-UMAMI-INFRA-HANDOFF.md.
# UMAMI_SRC=https://analytics.rn.thecoll.org/s.js
# UMAMI_WEBSITE_ID=
